I walk further in the market.
There is a flower stall there.
I stop in front of the stall.
An older woman sits there.
She is making a fresh flower garland.
There is a wonderful fragrance there.
I look at the garlands of yellow flowers.
The woman looks at me and smiles.
I do not ask the price.
But she herself tells the price.
She says, "The price of one garland is thirty rupees."
That price is reasonable.
I want one garland for the door of my home.
I am happy.
I say, "Madam, please give me one garland."
She gives the garland to me.
I give thirty rupees.
I put the garland in my cloth bag.
